# groff 1.23.0 segfaults when lintian renders a manual page, because of an
# AppArmor interaction with /usr/bin/man during lintian's own pipeline. It is
# unrelated to the content of the page: the same pipeline run by hand succeeds,
# and bisecting the page finds nothing that triggers it.
#
# Ubuntu bug LP #2055402, fixed upstream in groff 1.23.0-5; Ubuntu 24.04 still
# ships 1.23.0-3build2. When this override starts being reported as unused,
# the runner has a fixed groff and this file can go.
hdw4s-shared-sweep: groff-message

# The harden, sweep, watch and relay units are templates whose instance is a
# store's escaped path, and are wanted by THAT path's mount unit (%i.mount), so
# they start when the store is mounted and stop with it. Unusual, and the point.
hdw4s-shared-sweep: systemd-service-file-refers-to-unusual-wantedby-target %i.mount *
